   m=5: progression U = [0, 3, 4, 8]; violating pairs 1 (first [(0, 3)]); pair (0,4) violates: False; halved witnesses 3,0
   m=6: progression U = [0, 1, 4, 5, 8]; violating pairs 1 (first [(1, 5)]); pair (0,4) violates: False; halved witnesses 4,10
   m=7: progression U = [0, 3, 4, 7, 8, 12]; violating pairs 3 (first [(0, 4), (3, 7), (4, 7)]); pair (0,4) violates: True; halved witnesses 5,11
   m=8: progression U = [0, 1, 4, 5, 8, 9, 12]; violating pairs 5 (first [(0, 4), (0, 5), (1, 5)]); pair (0,4) violates: True; halved witnesses 6,12
   m = 5..60: progression always has a violating pair, and (0,4) violates with halved witnesses m-2, m+4 for m >= 7: True []
(3) cycle types of sigma_t sigma_t' (remark 'an alternative route that fails')
   direct composition = closed form for all m = 3..40 and all pairs: True
   m <= 40 NOT settled if the n-cycle case counts as settled: [5, 10, 13, 17, 25, 26, 29, 34, 37]
   m <= 24 NOT settled if only 'even order is impossible' is used: [4, 5, 10, 13, 17]
